{
  "_format": [
    "Step scenarios (lane X2), run with walk.sh run2 <name>. Each scenario has 'description', optional 'texts' and",
    "'tool_calls' (the mock server's scripted replies, as in scenarios.json), and 'steps', a list of objects with one",
    "action each:",
    "  load                 load 'texts' and 'tool_calls' now, after placeholders are known (default: at the start)",
    "  set_model {provider, model, key}   the debug set_model command (defaults: openai, walk-model, walk)",
    "  seed_app {name, data}  store a built app with bridge data; its id fills the placeholder <NAME>_ID (or 'as')",
    "  seed_widget {html, name, size, sources}   store a widget without a model",
    "  start TEXT           the home page's submit (FeedLocator.commands.submit)",
    "  notify {package, title, text}   the notification pipeline",
    "  confirm {item: last|draft|ID, yes}   a CONFIRM row's answer or a widget draft card tap",
    "  page home|history|widgets       approve, reject      mark (only rows and tasks after this count)",
    "  wait_row SPEC (timeout s), expect_row SPEC, expect_no_row SPEC, expect_rows SPEC with count",
    "      SPEC: kind, kind_in, state, state_in, text, text_contains, action_word, title",
    "  wait_task SPEC (timeout s), expect_tasks SPEC with count      SPEC: origin, state, state_in, goal, goal_contains",
    "  pause SECONDS",
    "Placeholders such as LINGO_ID or <LINGO_ID> are replaced in steps, texts and tool_calls.",
    "  suggestions on|off   change the notification suggestions switch",
    "  expect_requests N    assert the scripted model received exactly N requests",
    "RUN_ID is a fresh unique value for each run; use it in notification titles and goals for repeatable proposals."
  ],
  "proposal_accept_home": {
    "description": "F4.2, F5.6: a message makes a 'Do this?' row under its notification card; 'Do it' on the home page starts it. The same message after that makes a new proposal.",
    "texts": [
      {
        "triage": [
          {
            "match": {
              "title": "Alex RUN_ID",
              "package": "ai.opencyclone.testapp"
            },
            "result": "propose",
            "goal": "Reply to Alex RUN_ID that dinner at 7 works"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "triage": [
          {
            "match": {
              "title": "Alex RUN_ID",
              "package": "ai.opencyclone.testapp"
            },
            "result": "propose",
            "goal": "Reply to Alex RUN_ID that dinner at 7 works"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "tool_calls": [
      {
        "tool_call": {
          "thought": "Replied to Alex RUN_ID",
          "action_type": "finish"
        }
      }
    ],
    "steps": [
      {
        "start": "stop handling my notifications"
      },
      {
        "wait_row": {
          "kind": "SENTENCE"
        },
        "timeout": 20
      },
      {
        "mark": true
      },
      {
        "suggestions": "on"
      },
      {
        "notify": {
          "package": "ai.opencyclone.testapp",
          "title": "Alex RUN_ID",
          "text": "Are we still on for dinner at 7?"
        }
      },
      {
        "wait_row": {
          "kind": "CONFIRM",
          "state": "OPEN",
          "text": "Reply to Alex RUN_ID that dinner at 7 works?",
          "action_word": "Do it"
        },
        "timeout": 90
      },
      {
        "expect_tasks": {
          "origin": "notification",
          "state": "proposed"
        },
        "count": 1
      },
      {
        "confirm": {
          "item": "last",
          "yes": true
        }
      },
      {
        "wait_row": {
          "kind": "CONFIRM",
          "state": "ANSWERED"
        },
        "timeout": 20
      },
      {
        "wait_task": {
          "origin": "notification",
          "goal": "Reply to Alex RUN_ID that dinner at 7 works",
          "state_in": [
            "running",
            "done"
          ]
        },
        "timeout": 60
      },
      {
        "mark": true
      },
      {
        "notify": {
          "package": "ai.opencyclone.testapp",
          "title": "Alex RUN_ID",
          "text": "Are we still on for dinner at 7?"
        }
      },
      {
        "wait_row": {
          "kind": "CONFIRM",
          "state": "OPEN",
          "text": "Reply to Alex RUN_ID that dinner at 7 works?"
        },
        "timeout": 90
      },
      {
        "expect_tasks": {
          "origin": "notification",
          "state": "proposed",
          "goal": "Reply to Alex RUN_ID that dinner at 7 works"
        },
        "count": 1
      },
      {
        "confirm": {
          "item": "last",
          "yes": false
        }
      }
    ]
  },
